How the heck are you getting that measurment? My VRT19 measures about 18.9
inches visible. I don't hink DEC is out of line calling it 19 inches. But I
don't see how you come up with 17.5 inches!

First, industry standard has always been to state the full size of the CRT.
Back about 1970 the FTC mandated that TV screen sizes in the US be specified
only by the visible picture area. You could buy a 35" TV in Canada when the
identical set was 32" in the US. Since computer displays are not covered by the
FTC rule, I assume DEC can use whatever measure it prefers.

And I'm really curious about where you get that funny ruler.

