In article <CE2s9u.5os@jabba.ess.harris.com> smccoy@dr3r.ess.harris.com (Scott McCoy) writes:

>   On my new Alpha, when I send a message with a mixed mode address (such
>   as: bill%hisbox@some.gateway.org), I get the following error message:
>
>   post: unexpected response; [RPLY] 554 bill%hisbox@somegateway.org...
>   Unbalanced '<'
>   send: message not delivered to anyone

Yes indeed.  As far as I can tell this is a bug in the sendmail.cf that
comes with OSF.  A fix that works involves commenting out the following
line from rule S9.

R$*<@$+>$*             $:$1<@$[$2$]>$3                 canon'ize complex names

As far as I can tell getting rid of this line does not mess anything
else up.  I have tested this with the following sets of addresses and
they all work OK.

luchini@ic.ac.uk
luchini%ic.ac.uk@other.site
@other.site:luchini@ic.ac.uk
luchini%ic.ac.uk%site1%site2@site3
luchini@[146.201.223.41]

The @other.site:user@site seems to be the preferred form of addressing
of the sendmail.cf of OSF.  If you look at your "from" fields for messages
delivered from sites in mixed mode they show up in that format.  It also
works OK for sending using the out-of-the-box OSF sendmail.cf.

I do not know enough about sendmail rewriting rules to figure out what
the offending line was really supposed to do and why it bombs.


