> Hi folks, just a quick inquiry,
> has anyone ever considered writing a utility to find people using a vax ???
> you know, put together the line numbers with room numbers and processes 
> so that one can find out which people are in which rooms,

we used to have suach a utility here when there were hardwired terminals. very
easily done. It drew a nice map of the terminal room you were in with all
the other peoples logins marked on it. Because it could tell where you were it
also reversed the map according to which terminal you were sitting at and
which way you were facing.

We had a second program which did an animated display of people logging in and
out during the day. That proved quite amusing for looking at who came in and
where they sat - or more particularly who they sat next to.

These days its much harder due to the davent of PADs and terminal servers.
The best that the program can do these days is to say which room somebody is
sitting, or in large terminal rooms say which part of the room they are in.
Still works fairly well though.

