I suppose you've heard this before, but its new to me.
I'm going to have 2 Gigabytes maximum to back up.
Doing DAT versus Exabyte comparison. Anyone have anything to add? 
Thanks.
------------------------------------------------------------------------
The most reasonable two remaining options are DAT (4mm) tape and
Exabyte  (8mm) tape. Transfer rates are appx 250KB and 500 KB per
second respectively; at those rates 1 GB can be backed up in 67 or 33
minutes respectively.

A 4GB SCSI DAT unit from DEC (TLZ06) runs $1,899 list price while a 
DEC 5GB SCSI Exabyte unit (TKZ09) costs $4,995 list. Third party these
prices go down to appx $1,095 and $2,295. For the increase in speed
that the Exabyte provides over DAT, the more than doubling in price
probably makes the Exabyte not worth it for us. We will have maximum
of just over 2 Gb  to backup and the difference between 1/2 hour and 1
hour is not that  significant.

The 4GB DAT unit uses 90 meter tapes (Verbatim appx $17 each) while
the 5GB  Exabyte unit uses 112 meter tapes (Verbatim appx $12 each).
------------------------------------------------------------------------

