Hi all,

Has anyone come across the problem of using keys in X,
specifically KeyPress and KeyRelease?

I've seen this problem in a couple of X games, XBoing and Xpilot
(there may be more). No matter what keys you assign to move left or
right, they don't work.

It seems that when you press a key in the main Qwerty cluster,
two Xevents (press and release) are sent despite you having not let
go of the key. (You can check this using xev.)
This creates problems in games where the program must
detect when you want to move an object.

Does anyone out there worked out how to get around this?
Is it the keyboards or the DECWindows X server?

FYI,
I run XBoing from a remote unix box, exporting the DISPLAY back.
I also do this with xpilot though I now have a beta port which does
the same thing.
The problem occurs on all the DEC machines we have here:
VAX 3100s and Alpha 3000/400s which have LK201 and LK401 keyboards.

Peter - peterc@v2.ph.man.ac.uk

