Sorry, but there seems to be some confusion due to an unfortunate
choice of acronyms...

The POLYCENTER Advanced File System (a local file system which does
logging for rapid crash recovery, can span multiple disks, allows
online resizing, and other goodies) is NOT the same thing as Transarc
Corporation's AFS (a networked distributed filesystem based on work
done on the Andrew project at Carnegie-Mellon University).  The online
documentation CD I have (dated August 1993) does not refer to the
POLYCENTER Advanced Filesystem as "AFS".  Perhaps an earlier revision
of the documentation did so by mistake.

I personally don't know if Transarc has AFS for DEC OSF/1 available
yet or not, or what their plans if any are.

