Well said -- It is impossible.

A year or so back we slipped behind in Ultrix version and had to
reinstall from scratch at 4.2 ( or possible 4.1) and only DECnet Phase
V was supplied.  So we assumed that we had to use it and ran it for
about 2 months before abandoning it and reinstalling DECnet Phase IV.

During that time I spent about 50% of my time on it, TSC spend a half
day logged it on two occasions to try and sort out problems, we had
continual incomprehensible error massages, starting DECnet often
locked up the machine requiring a power off reset, gethostbyname did
not work, etc etc...

I accept that it may now have less bugs but the documentation supplied
with Ultrix is awful. What is desperately needed is an ncp to ncl
conversion table for simple things like ncp define object, ncp show
line counters etc. I understand that VMS documentation comes with such
info but us poor folks running Ultrix just have to guess.

I am having to upgrade to 4.3A to support R4400 chips and understand
that support is being dropped for Phase IV :-(. I cannot face Phase V
again so am currently converting 20 odd PC's to TCP/IP then I will
happily say bye bye to DECnet.

Just my Personnal Opinion.

Tim

