All DECnet-OSI implementation ship a utility called decnet_migrate which
(among it's bazillion other things) can translate most NCP command to NCL.

decnet_migrate> conv comm "define object foo number 240 file /usr/etc/food defa
ult user guest"

# *** Converting the following NCP command to NCL:
#     define object foo number 240 file /usr/etc/food default user guest
#     NCL initialization files have replaced the permanent database
#     Conversion assumes command applies to volatile database
create node 0 session control application {{{foo}}}
set node 0 session control application {{{foo}}} address={number=240}, image nam
e={{{/usr/etc/food}}}, user name={{{guest}}}
