Well, if you have them :-). DEC had a funny way with the manuals for our
first ULTRIXes: the ones with Phase IV only had the manuals for Phase V and
vice versa. I'm greatful they've changed this policy now!

> There is nonetheless a lot of new terminology, new concepts, etc., to learn.

As DEC competes with Big Blue, and the latter is good at creating new
terminology, this is only natural :-).

[ ... ]

> A workstation with a couple of 48-line (at least) DECterms, one for browsing
> NCL HELP and the other for actually doing NCL, is a must.  Also plan to keep
> several square feet of desk space free, for the various manuals that will all
