This understates one big advantage of Exabytes for sites that do a lot of
backups: the tapes (which hold more than 2x the 4mm tapes) are much cheaper.
You should be able to get reasonable 8mm backup tapes for under $3 each,
as long as you use the right consumer videotape (e.g. don't use Sony).

George Goble of Purdue, who does a lot of Exabyte backups, took the trouble
to try several kinds of consumer videotapes to see which ones would work well.
The best was the Fuji P6-120MP DS, which has a much lower write retry rate
even than the expensive Sony QC-112m data tapes.  We've recently switched
to the Fuji tape ourselves.  Exabyte recommends that you use Exabyte certified
data tapes but a lot of sites ignore this advice without reporting ill effects.


