In article <277d5a$a8n@walton.maths.tcd.ie>, rjwalsh@maths.tcd.ie (Robert Walsh) writes:
> I'm using Ultrix 4.2 (Rev. 96). If anyone has experienced problems
> like this before, or has ANY idea what's going wrong with the
> drives/controller, I'd appreciate hearing from them.

  I assume you have an RQDX3 controller, and possibly a BA123 box or some
non-DEC cabinet. The RQDX3 supports a total of 4 drives, which can be any
combination of floppies (RX33, RX50 [counts as 2 drives]) and RD-series
hard disks. Each drive needs to have a unique unit number. If two hard
disks have the same unit number, the format on at least one of them will
be corrupted when the drive is accessed.

  If you have a BA123 with an M9058 signal distribution board, this should
not happen unless somebody has done something very non-standard (like a
daisy-chain on the 34-pin cable), since the default M9058 configuration
handles drive selection based on what connector pair is used.

