stevev@npg-sd.SanDiegoCA.NCR.COM (Steve Van Daele) asks:

| Can someone explain the vt100 "compose" key/function.

The VT100 did not have a compose key, this came much later as part of
the LK200 keyboard.  The compose key is used to form characters that
are not on the keyboard.  Most of these are international characters,
but some are useful symbols - compose+c+o will get you the Copyright
symbol for instance.  Compose+0+^ will get you the degree symbol. 
The compose key is used by pressing compose, and then pressing two
following characters (they do not need to be held down at once, and
are usually order insensitive).

A VT200, VT300, VT400 or VT500 users guide will give you the complete
list of compose sequences.

The compose key is simulated on most X11 systems by pressing ALT-SPACE



