If backups are your main reason for purchasing one of the above stated devices,
then I suggest you go with the 4mm product.  4mm offers high capacity at a very
low cost per MB when compared to other BACKUP medias.  If that is what you are
in search of.  If you are concerned with media shelf life, quick data retrival,
random access of data files, or even the capability to boot your system off of
this media then I suggest optical.  There are higher capacities available above
the 600MB you have listed.  HP offers a 1.2 GB (Formatted 512/Bytes sectors) 
optical disk and manufacturers such as Maxoptics and Hitachi are offering 2+ GB
per platter all at reasonable prices. 

Both technologies are also available in autochangers, where robotics
automatically move media in and out of the drive based upon commands issued by
the user.  This configuration is dependant upon your future storage 
requirements.

