NNTP-Posting-Host: porter.mit.edu

I noticed a DECstation 5000/200 was running faster than a 5000/133 even
though the processor in the 133 is faster.  I wasn't measuring I/O so
the half speed turbochannel isn't the problem.

I wrote a short loop in assembly language to store to memory and found that
the /133 could only sustain a rate of 1 store per 7 cycles, while the /200
could store a word every cycle.  (Stores were to the same locations each
loop iteration.)

Based on this test I conclude that the /200 has a write-back cache and
the /133 has a write-through cache.  Is this correct?

-- 
