In article <26qgtm$95f@gamera.umd.edu>,
Michael F. Santangelo <mike@starburst.umd.edu> wrote:
>I don't unfortunately have a manual for this TQK50 controller, but I
>need to know the dip switch settings to change it to the /secondary/
>TMSCP CSR address.  I have a device that wants to be at 774500 before
>it.  Would be very appreciative to anyone who could provide it,
>thanks.
>

There is a row of 11 jumpers on the board. A12-A2 where A2 is closest
to the board edge. These jumpers make up a binary number. 1 is jumper
installed. The bits A1 and A0 are zero. To find the CSR address you
take the binary number you get and add it to the octal number
17760000. If you set the jumpers A12-A2 to 00001000001, you get
the binary number 0 000 100 000 100 which is 00404 octal. The CSR
address would then be 17760404.

Hope this helps
-- 
Stig (venaas@nvg.unit.no)


