In article <1a.141.2558.0N51A8CF@iol.ie>, mike.mccrohan@iol.ie (Mike Mccrohan)
writes:
|>
|>Similarly, the 8500 was  a single proc machine, the 8550 was a faster
|>version or the 8550 (actually it was really the other way around - the
|>8500 was a slugged 8550). The 8550 cpu was the same as was in the 8700.
|>Two processors in the 8700 made it an 8800.
