The LK201 keyboard doesn't have an ALT key.  The ALT function is necessary to
support Motif properly.  For compatibility with keyboards on other systems (most
notably PCs), it was decided that the key marked COMPOSE, which is where the
ALT key is on other keyboards, would be used for the ALT function and that
the COMPOSE function would be moved to ALT-SPACE.

So, to initiate a COMPOSE sequence on a LK201 in DECwrite, you hold down the
COMPOSE (ALT) key and press the space bar.

--PSW


