The XMedia software will allow you to use this audio port.  The license
for this was bundled with the Personal DECstations, I think, so you
should be able to find it on one of your CDROMs.  It won't help with
your problem though, see below.

|>I found the dectalk software on gatekeeper but it refers to
|>the dectalk daemon and the device /dev/ttyh0 both of which
|>I cannot find.

The DECtalk software that you found is just a simple client/server
setup to allow multiple network clients easily access a serial line
DECtalk (DTC01 or DTC03).  You would need to have one of these 
connected to your computer for this software to be useful for you.
It looks like it defaults to /dev/ttyh0 as the serial port that
it uses to talk to the device.

