    You need to read the documentation on the arguments to $BRKTHRU more
closely, either via the  Fine  Manuals,  BOOKREADER,  or simply from DCL
with HELP SYSTEM $BRKTHRU.

    First, the arguments "sndtyp" and  "reqid"  must be passed by value.
Secondly,  you  haven't supplied an event flag (so that event flag 0  is
used by default), so you'd better use  $BRKTHRUW.   Thirdly,  while  you
checked  the  return  status of $BRKTHRU itself, you haven't checked the
completion status  returned  in  the  IOSB,  nor  have  you  declared it
properly,  it  is  a _quadword_.  There's also a good  chance  that  the
device name, "sendto" argument, needs to be upper-cased: this isn't  DCL
:-) The slightly modified code (sorry, I haven't tested it) would be:

	.
	.
	INTEGER*2 IOSB(4)
	.
	.
	RETVAL = SYS$BRKTHRUW (, 'this is a test', '_FTA82:', 
     >          	       %VAL(BRK$C_DEVICE), IOSB,, 
     >			       %VAL(BRK$C_USER7),,,)
	WRITE (6,*) 'RETVAL=',RETVAL
	IF (RETVAL)  WRITE (6,*) '    (Success)'
	WRITE (6,*) 'IOSB(1)=', IOSB(1)
	IF (IOSB(1)) WRITE (6,*) '    (Success)'
	.
	.


