The AdvFS or DEC advanced filesystem is actually called the POLYCENTER 
Advanced File System. From the DEC OSF/1 V1.3 Software Product Description 
(SPD#41.61.03):

    The POLYCENTER Advanced File System is a local file system that uses
    journaling to recover from unplanned system restarts, such as power
    failures, significantly faster than the standard UNIX File System (UFS).
    In addition to fast restart, POLYCENTER Advanced File System improves
    the integrity and consistency of file system structures; extends file
    sizes to greater than 2 Gigabytes; enhances backup utilities by writ-
    ing data to archive media in compressed form; and enables fast file
    creation and deletion.

    The right to use the POLYCENTER Advanced File System is granted by the
    DEC OSF/1 V1.3 license. However, binaries and on-line documentation
    are separately available on the Digital Consolidated Distribution CD-
    ROM, rather than on the DEC OSF/1 CD-ROM.

For customers who require greater system availability, on-line file system
resizing, and added performance, Digital offers the POLYCENTER Advanced File
System Utilities as an incremental layered product.  For more information on
part numbers and prices (USA anyway) for both of these products, look at:

