Dear Helpful Netters:

I'm currently having a problem with the DEC cc compiler an passing floats.
What I would like to do is define a function in K&R style but in a header
file give it a full function prototye with parameters.  (The reason is
I would like to integrate a K&R style library with some C++ code.)  The
following program demonstrates the problem I'm having.  It is done completely
with cc (no C++).  The problem is that the K&R definition expects a float
of size 8 instead of size 4.  The man page would indicate that this is
because DEC cc "promote[s] expressions of type float to type double".  However,
the "-f" flag which is suppose to stop the "promotion" doesn't seem to work.
Therefore I will guess I have a bad version of cc and need to upgrade to a
more recent version. 

1) Can anyone tell me if I am right or else what is wrong and how to fix it?
2) If I'm right, can you tell me what version of cc I need?

Thank you for your time and help.  Please E-mail. I'll post results if 
requested to.

Here is the example:

