valerie@cs.umass.edu (Valerie Caro) writes:


>    I am using some rz58 disks as secondary swap space for
>some DECstations running Ultrix 4.2 and 4.3. I would like
>to change the disks to spin up on power up, but I can't
>find the way to do this with the rzdisk command. Could someone
>who has done this please tell me the exact commands I need
>to set this.

Your most easy approach is to add a simple jumper on the drive.
No need to mess with software. So: place a jumper on 4th position
from the right. Positions 1, 2 3, are the drive select/SCSI ID
jumpers, the 4th is the one you want.

Note that the software spinup is used to avoid heavy inrush currents
on the powersupply, so watch your step if you want all the drives
to spinup at once.

