the following is from my experience using DECwrite on Ultrix, but it
should be the same for VMS as well (because the DECwrite v2.0 User's
Guide is system independent and it says that DECwrite works the same on
VMS, Ultrix and Sun).

to compose a character, press and hold the 'compose character' key and
then press the 'space bar', release both and type in your compose
characters. see WRITE$EXAMPLES:KEYBOARD.DOC.

in some window managers, like mwm on Ultrix, i had to press and hold the
'compose character' key and then press the 'space bar' _twice_ before i
could type in the compose characters. 

